# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Read from the *context root*, which `render.yaml` sets to `ZacoAgents_Chris`, so this file
# governs the hosted build as well as the local one.
#
# Two different reasons appear below and they are worth keeping apart. Most entries are things
# the image does not need -- they would be uploaded, hashed and thrown away. A few are things that
# would be actively wrong to ship: a local `.env`, or a frontend bundle built on somebody's laptop
# instead of by the `frontend` stage.

# --- version control and local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode
.venv
venv

# --- Python build and cache droppings -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
*.egg-info

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` is a *local* file. Hosted configuration comes from the environment (D3), and an `.env`
# baked into an image would silently win over it.
.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- build artefacts that must be made inside the image, not copied in ---------------------------
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
# The bundle. Built by the `frontend` stage from source; a developer's local build would otherwise
# ship instead of the one this Dockerfile made, and the two are not always the same.
zaco/web/spa
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- not part of the application ----------------------------------------------------------------
# None of this is COPYed by the Dockerfile. It is excluded so it is not uploaded and hashed on
# every deploy, and so a change to a document does not invalidate the build cache.
tests
PersonalTest
docs
*.md
docker
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml

# The supplied agent reports. They are the exercise's input and the fixtures the suite reads; the
# running system is given documents through the interface, and reads nothing from here.
data

# The blank workbook template. Only `workbook/account-sales-book.xlsx` is COPYed, as the seed for
# an empty disk.
workbook/template.xlsx
